## Find the right kind of term

| What you need | Reference |
| --- | --- |
| An explanation of a concept such as entity, automation, app or template | [Complete official-glossary mapping](ha-glossary.html) |
| A domain, helper type, raw state, attribute or device-class label | [Entity and state language](entity-and-state-language.html) |
| A dashboard, action, Assist, Energy, security, Settings or configuration term | [Interface and configuration terminology](interface-terminology.html) |
| A route or interface surface and its native-versus-civica coverage | [Native interface coverage record](../reference/ha-interface-coverage.json) |
| Stable identifiers and exact source pointers for automation or review | [Terminology JSON](../reference/ha-terminology.json) |

The reference pages have named sections and expandable entries. Use the page's contents links or your browser's find command to locate a name or literal key. No script is needed to read an entry or follow its source link.

## Choose wording by purpose

| Context | What to write | What to preserve |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A household control | The supported action and actual target, such as “Turn on Nain’s reading lamp” | The supplied name and actual capability |
| A native navigation step | The actual translated control name for the stated version | Native wording, even when it is more technical than the surrounding explanation |
| First use of a necessary concept | The native term followed by a short explanation | Its distinction from similar concepts |
| Diagnostics or configuration | The exact field, value, path or identifier in code styling | Case, dots, underscores, spaces and punctuation required by the syntax |
| An older instruction | Explain the current name while identifying the historical term | Literal old keys and saved routes unless a verified migration changes them |

Do not run a global replacement from “entity” to “device”, “notification” to “message”, or “service” to “action”. These words can have different technical meanings. “Service” may describe a non-device information source, an older action label, or a backend API. Specify which meaning the task uses.

