The official glossary mapping covers all **83** source entries: **72** Home Assistant concepts and **11** data or template types. The entity-platform mapping covers all **45** entries in the pinned Core registry. The card, feature, selector and view counts come from native dispatch registries and include technical or historical keys where the source includes them. They are not counts of public editor choices or maintained civica components.

The supplementary domain map also covers all **15** additional state domains identified by the native row and dialog census, plus **Plant, Zone and Schedule** from the existing guide topics and official integration references. It reuses existing glossary and helper entries where they already explain the concept. Inventory counts can therefore overlap; they are not a sum of unique terms. These domains remain separate from the 45-platform denominator.

The nine named helper types and Settings destinations cover the stated English translation subtrees. Other helper integrations exist. Native state labels cover the selected platform translation subtrees, including device-class and attribute context; they do not enumerate every integration-specific value. The separate [interface census](../reference/ha-interface-coverage.json) owns route and surface counts.

This is a complete mapping of these **named, dated inventories**, not a promise to contain every vendor term, custom card, integration parameter, translated sentence or future release. A missing term needs a source-backed addition, not a guessed translation.

## Keep translations and technical keys distinct

Native English source labels are shown so an author can identify the reference. They are not instructions to force English into another locale. Keep the actual native translation and the person's supplied names. Explain an unfamiliar term near the task, and review any new authored translation in that language.

The native-label tables distinguish a raw state, attribute property, attribute value, device-class translation key and translation fallback key. In particular, `_` is a default entry in a translation file. It is **not** an entity ID or a device-class setting to paste into configuration.

## Source freshness and writing guidance

On 12 November 2026, all **37** previously hashed NHS, Home Office and GOV.UK writing sources returned exactly the same HTML bytes as the 11 November review. This establishes that those retrieved pages did not change between the two checks; it does not establish that every sentence in this repository complies with them.

The current [Plain English Campaign free-guides index](https://www.plainenglish.co.uk/free-guides) and [SCULPT framework page](https://www.worcestershire.gov.uk/council-services/business/digital-worcestershire/sculpt-accessibility/what-sculpt) were also checked. They had no previous recorded HTML hash, so this guide does not claim their bytes were unchanged. The earlier scoped PDF review remains dated 11 November; this refresh does not claim every linked PDF was reread.

No change to the **68 frozen writing rules** was required by this source refresh. The terminology explanations are original civica content. Plain English word lists, SCULPT artwork and endorsement claims are not reproduced.

