## Maintain an entry

1. Identify the task and whether the text is a native label, supplied name, technical value or authored explanation.
2. Read its official source at the supported version. Check the actual integration when a capability or state is conditional.
3. Preserve the native name and literal value; write a separate first-use explanation and the most likely confusion.
4. Record the stable entry ID, source, checked date, version and inventory membership. Retain historical keys where saved configuration still depends on them.
5. Check the example in ordinary, missing and ambiguous states, then review the rendered page and relevant user task. Record those checks separately from source inspection.

The [terminology JSON](../reference/ha-terminology.json) contains the full source-refresh record and exact inventory members. The [content review chapter](content-review.html) explains evidence, exceptions and meaningful change notes.
